from itertools import permutations
from statskit import median, mean
# order-independence across every permutation, odd and even lengths
for base in ([5,1,3],[4,1,3,2],[9,9,9],[1,2,3,4,5,6]):
    results = {median(list(p)) for p in permutations(base)}
    assert len(results)==1, (base, results)
    print(base, '->', results.pop(), 'stable across all', len(list(permutations(base))), 'permutations')
# empty-input error behaviour preserved
for fn in (mean, median):
    try:
        fn([]); print('FAIL: no error')
    except ValueError as e: print(fn.__name__, '([]) still raises ValueError:', e)
print('generator input:', median(x for x in [5,1,3]))
